Description
In this lab, you will learn how Ansible templates (Jinja2) help eliminate hard-coded configuration values by dynamically injecting variables into configuration files.

Instead of manually editing configuration files for every server, you will define variables once and let Ansible generate the final configuration automatically. This is a foundational skill for scalable and maintainable automation.

You are provided with an Ansible control node and a managed node (server1).

Your task is to:

Create an NGINX configuration using a Jinja2 template

Define variables inside the playbook

Deploy the rendered configuration to the remote server

Lab Objective
How Jinja2 templates work in Ansible

How variables replace hard-coded values

How Ansible generates final configuration files dynamically

